1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:11,782
In this video you will learn how to run a business with
NTSOne. Create a business, put your products online, take an
order from a customer, and send an invoice.

2
00:00:12,382 --> 00:00:31,493
Open Businesses and choose New Business. Enter its name,
email, phone, address and a short description. Your business
gets its own workspace, with tabs for the order form, orders,
quotations, invoices, receipts, business cards, bookkeeping
and analytics.

3
00:00:32,093 --> 00:00:47,185
Open the Order Form tab and add the items you sell, each with
a name and a price. You can also add pictures and videos. Then
add the questions customers must answer, such as their name,
phone number and delivery address.

4
00:00:47,785 --> 00:01:01,117
Save and publish the form, then choose Start taking orders.
Your order page now has its own link and a QR code, so
customers can open it from a message, a poster or a social
media post.

5
00:01:01,717 --> 00:01:12,920
This is your online shop. Customers see your business details,
browse your products, and add what they want to their order.
The total updates as they go.

6
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:27,977
At checkout the customer enters their details, reviews the
order, and confirms it. When payments are turned on, they pay
with mobile money at this point. They then get an order number
and a copy of their order to keep.

7
00:01:28,577 --> 00:01:44,479
Back in your workspace, the Orders tab lists every order. Open
one to see the items, the customer's answers and its history.
Choose a new status, add a note, and update it, and the
customer can be emailed at each step.

8
00:01:45,079 --> 00:02:03,031
To bill a client, open Invoices and choose New invoice. Enter
the client, the items, quantities and prices. Save it, and you
can print it, download it as a PDF, or send it by email.
Receipts and quotations work the same way.

9
00:02:03,631 --> 00:02:14,538
The same tabs let you create receipts and quotations, design
business cards with a QR code, and follow your orders, money
invoiced and money received in Analytics.

10
00:02:15,138 --> 00:02:23,876
That is how you run a business with NTSOne. Use this video as
your guide, and watch the next video to learn about payments.
